---
description: Shell/SSH commands must never print or paste API keys or secrets
alwaysApply: true
---

# No secret reveal in commands

Jab agent user ko Mac Terminal / EC2 SSH / docker / curl / node commands de:

## Never
- `echo $VYAPARAPI_API_KEY` / `printenv | grep KEY` / secrets ko stdout pe dump
- Command mein raw key/secret paste (Coolify values, bot tokens, webhook secrets)
- User se bolo “key yahan paste karo” — Coolify / local `.env` pe daalein

## Always (debug / verify)
- Sirf **presence / length / boolean**:
  - `echo KEY=${VYAPARAPI_API_KEY:+set}`
  - `console.log("keyLen="+k.length)`
  - `sameAsBest=(a===b)` without printing `a`/`b`
- API response mein agar key echo ho sakti ho to `slice` / redact; full env dump mat mango
- User output paste kare to assume safe — agar unhone galti se key bhej di to **dobara mat quote** karo; rotate bol do

## Examples

```bash
# ❌ BAD
sudo docker exec "$cid" sh -c 'echo $BESTAPI_API_KEY'

# ✅ GOOD
sudo docker exec "$cid" sh -c 'echo BESTAPI_KEY=${BESTAPI_API_KEY:+set} LEN=${#BESTAPI_API_KEY}'
```

```bash
# ✅ GOOD — fetch uses env inside container; only logs status/body slice
node -e 'const k=(process.env.VYAPARAPI_API_KEY||"").trim(); console.log("keyLen="+k.length); fetch("https://api.vyaparapi.com/public/balance?api_key="+encodeURIComponent(k)).then(r=>r.text()).then(t=>console.log(t.slice(0,300)))'
```
